 methods=r'''For each original flood, the initial closed-road set F was fixed. The original ten-road set used equal weights on normalized descending minimum ranks of pre-flood physical flow and betweenness, (|F|−rank)/(|F|−1), with archived score/flow/betweenness/ID tie rules. Prespecified Flow-only and Betweenness-only alternatives selected ten roads from F. A diagnostic one-road swap was allowed only when |F|>10 and both alternatives reproduced the original set. Identical physical sets and restored subsets were deduplicated before UE computation. For a selected set E, with |E|=10, W_E(empty)=0 and W_E(S)=min_(e in S)[W_E(S without e)+C(S without e)], where C(S)=TSTT_UE(S)/T0−1. The conditional optimum is W_E(E)/10; it weights S0–S9 equally and excludes S10. The recurrence is an application of established cumulative UE recovery/Bellman formulations, not a new mathematical structure. The reference is exact for the supplied cost table conditional on E; it does not optimize the portfolio globally.'''
 insert=f'''# Proposed manuscript/Supplement changes for Comment5.5\n\nPrepared text only. Original Word, Supplement and previous replies are unchanged. Targets below use section names, with final page/line numbers pending author merge. Replace broad complete-recovery claims rather than adding repetitive qualifications.\n\n## Methods: preselection and conditional reference\n\n{methods}\n\n## Results: limited selection sensitivity\n\nSeven of the ten original floods allowed different ten-road sets. The prespecified rules produced ten distinct alternatives; five improved and five worsened the conditional cumulative optimum. Better tested sets existed for scenarios1003,1004 and1008. In scenario1003, Flow-only reduced the objective by{r1003.selection_gain_pct:.4f}% relative to the original set, equivalent to{r1003.delta_model_ATT_minutes:.3f} model-implied average-stage minutes per trip. This is sensitivity within a finite collection of tested sets, not a global joint recovery optimum. Completion of the original ten interventions left one or two closed roads in seven floods, with10–18 initially open wet roads still degraded across the ten floods. The best tested cumulative and terminal sets differed in scenarios1004 and1009.\n\n## Discussion: replace the complete recovery interpretation\n\nA low ordering regret within a fixed recovery set does not establish that the set itself is optimal. Selected-intervention completion is not whole-network recovery. Restoring all initially closed roads also leaves the initially open wet roads degraded, and UE re-equilibration can make the terminal TSTT comparison nonmonotonic. The signed static-state decomposition is not causal loss attribution or an operational recommendation. The synthetic, always-connected, fixed-demand testbed retains single-crew equal-duration actions and immediate restoration. Crew access and safety, dynamic flood/traffic, unserved demand, critical facilities, distributional welfare and engineering costs remain outside the model.\n\n## Supplement: mathematical identities and full evidence\n\nIn addition to the predecessor recurrence, give V_E(empty)=C(empty) and V_E(S)=min_(e in S)[V_E(S without e)+1[S≠E]C(S)], so J*=V_E(E)/10. Any path entering S last through e has a predecessor ordering of S without e; minimizing that earlier cost and adding the pre-action state's cost proves W by induction over |S|. The endpoint-excluded V expression enumerates exactly the same ten stage costs. The reverse remaining-actions recurrence independently verifies the value. This reasoning assumes static set-dependent costs and does not assert arbitrary traffic path independence. Cite the established cumulative UE/Bellman work consistently with the novelty correction; retain the original5.1 reference record rather than invent a new citation.\n\nselection_gain_pct=100(J_A0−J_E)/J_A0, positive for an improvement; A0_selection_gap_to_best_tested_pct=100(J_A0−J_best_tested)/J_best_tested. The denominators differ. The signed model ATT difference equals0.6T0_raw(J_A0−J_E)/Q minutes with Q=360600. These are model-implied average static-stage trip times, not measured journeys or real cumulative repair losses.\n\nFor endpoints, report TSTT(S10_E)−T0=[TSTT(S10_E)−TSTT(F)]+[TSTT(F)−T0] in raw and veh·h units, retaining negative terms. TSTT(F) restores only originally closed roads; it is not a fully dry network. Include the full20 portfolio rows,31 label aliases,10 counterfactuals,15,239 unique states,20480 DP state channels and raw new flow vectors/query logs.\n\n## Evidence placement/compression record\n\n| Finding | Role | Placement |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Three selectable floods have better tested sets | Materially limits conclusions | Brief Results and main conditional-plan qualification |\n| Five improving and five worsening alternatives | Complete direction reporting | Results sentence; all per-scenario values in SI |\n| Endpoint residual and conflicting objectives | Changes practical interpretation | Results/Discussion; full decomposition in SI |\n| Alias and source/context/hash checks | Provenance | SI/data archive |\n| Established Bellman structure | Attribution | Methods with existing verified5.1 bibliography |\n| Original Full/UE-only comparison | Existing evidence | Preserve prior findings; no replacement by this oracle comparison |\n\n中文合并提示：不写we optimized road portfolio selection或globally optimal recovery plan；用tested alternative preselection rules under conditional exact UE-DP for the fixed ten-action scope。4.1—5.4结果不覆盖。\n'''
 write('Manuscript_insertions_Comment5.5_EN.md',insert)
 write('figures/Figure_captions_EN.md','''# Figure captions\n\n**Figure_R1_5_5_selection_sensitivity.** Conditional cumulative-objective sensitivity to prespecified ten-road preselection rules. Panel a shows selection_gain=100(J*_A0−J*_E)/J*_A0; panel b converts the same paired objective difference to model-implied mean-static-stage trip-time gain in minutes. Positive values favor the alternative. Blue circles indicate Flow-only, orange squares Betweenness-only and the green triangle the eligible diagnostic swap. Rules that reproduce A0 remain as zero-valued aliases; the swap is not defined outside its prespecified trigger. Gray bands identify the three floods with exactly ten initial closures and no alternative legal ten-road set. The study comprises ten original independent synthetic floods, seven with selection freedom; alternative rules are not extra independent floods. Every objective is a post-study full-information conditional UE-DP reference, not a budgeted run of Full or a global selected-set optimum. No significance test is performed. Sources: Table_rule_label_results.csv and Table_portfolio_DP_comparison.csv.\n\n**Figure_R1_5_5_terminal_residual.** Selected-intervention completion and residual disruption. Panel a reports terminal model-implied ATT; panel b reports initially closed roads that remain unrepaired. Original and distinct alternative ten-road sets are compared with a static counterfactual restoring every originally closed road. Multiple alternatives may share the same residual count; horizontal offsets separate records without changing their values. Initially open wet roads retain their original flood effects even in the counterfactual, so zero remaining closures does not imply an all-dry network. All signed differences, including a nonmonotonic endpoint comparison in scenario1004, are retained in the data tables. Raw TNTP time units are0.01h, Q=360600, and displayed minutes are static model outputs rather than observed travel times or cumulative engineering losses. Endpoint cost has zero weight in the ten-stage cumulative objective. Sources: Table_terminal_residual_by_portfolio.csv and Table_allclosed_counterfactual.csv.\n''')
 write('QA_validation.md',f'''# Final QA\n\n{status}, {npassed}/{ntotal} checks. Full named checks with actual/expected values and evidence are in final_validation.json.\n\n- Prospective selection/input freeze and23 pre-solve authority checks passed. All20 distinct sets have1024 states; seven choice scenarios and three no-choice cases retained.\n- New UE4999/4999, failure0, RG≤1e-9; accepted reuse10240. All4999 independently reconstructed BPR flow costs/conservation pass;57 separate Python heap-Dijkstra checks pass.\n-20 DPs pass W/V/reverse/explicit trajectory checks;10 A0 references and5.2 physical endpoints regress;35 deterministic exhaustive/sentinel/shift tests pass.\n- Final CSV validation independently reconstructs masks, objectives, selection-gain signs/denominators, minute units, best-tested values and raw/veh·h endpoint decompositions.\n- {preserve['unchanged_files']}/{preserve['checked_files']} old-source hashes unchanged, including5.2({preserve['comment5_2_files']}files) and5.4({preserve['comment5_4_files']}files); Git identity/differences outside new directory unchanged.\n- Both actual PNGs reviewed; embedded PDF fonts min7pt; PNG600dpi; two panel-alignment gates≤1.5pt PASS and two PDF collision audits0FAIL/0WARN. Source preflight only WARN is no TIFF, which supplied protocol does not request.\n- Initial analysis parser typo corrected before producing numeric summaries; initial log retained. It did not change prospective settings, solver, parameters or UE data, and caused no new UE rerun.\n- Finite alternatives, nonmonotonic endpoint and all unfavorable outcomes retained. No global optimality, surrogate superiority, empirical disaster/safety or master-merge completion claim.\n''')
